IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 8 -- Terms and references in Acts, second group (ss 33 to 35A).
-- References to Ministers, departments, chief executives, States and Territories, officers, chair titles, Queensland, and persons with an interest in land.
-- The Public Sector Act 2022 is not among the sources, so whether an entity is a department of government under it is an input.

§ `Part 8 -- Terms and references in Acts (ss 33 to 35A)`

§§ `s 33 -- References to Ministers`

-- src:651 | (1) In an Act—
-- src:652 | (a) a reference to a Minister is a reference to a Minister of the State; and
@ref s 33(1) (src:651-652)
GIVEN `the person is a Minister of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a Minister is a reference to the person (s 33(1)(a))` IS
    JUST `the person is a Minister of the State`

-- src:653 | (b) a reference to a particular Minister by title, or to the Minister without specifying a particular Minister by title, includes a reference to another Minister, or member of the Executive Council, who is acting for the Minister.
@ref s 33(1) (src:653-653)
GIVEN `the reference is to a particular Minister by title, or to the Minister without specifying a particular Minister by title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is another Minister, or a member of the Executive Council, who is acting for the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference includes a reference to the person (s 33(1)(b))` IS
    IF `the reference is to a particular Minister by title, or to the Minister without specifying a particular Minister by title` AND `the person is another Minister, or a member of the Executive Council, who is acting for the Minister`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Which Minister a reference to the Minister is a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister administering the provision`
    `the Minister who administers the provision in relation to the relevant matter`
    `any 1 of the Ministers who administer the provision in relation to the relevant matter`
    `any 1 of the Ministers who administer the provision`

-- (2): (a) the Minister administering the provision; (b) if different Ministers administer it for different matters: (i) one Minister for the matter -- that Minister; (ii) 2 or more -- any 1 of them;
-- (c) if (b) does not apply and 2 or more Ministers administer the provision -- any 1 of them.
-- src:654 | (2) In a provision of an Act, a reference to the Minister without specifying a particular Minister by title is a reference to—
-- src:655 | (a) the Minister administering the provision; or
-- src:656 | (b) if, for the time being, different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters—
-- src:657 | (i) if only 1 Minister administers the provision in relation to the relevant matter—the Minister; or
-- src:658 | (ii) if 2 or more Ministers administer the provision in relation to the relevant matter—any 1 of the Ministers; or
-- src:659 | (c) if paragraph (b) does not apply and, for the time being, 2 or more Ministers administer the provision—any 1 of the Ministers.
@ref s 33(2) (src:654-659)
GIVEN `different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how many Ministers administer the provision in relation to the relevant matter` IS A NUMBER
      `how many Ministers administer the provision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which Minister a reference to the Minister is a reference to`
DECIDE `which Minister a reference to the Minister without specifying a particular Minister by title is a reference to (s 33(2))` IS
    IF `different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters`
    THEN IF `how many Ministers administer the provision in relation to the relevant matter` EQUALS 1
         THEN JUST `the Minister who administers the provision in relation to the relevant matter`
         ELSE IF `how many Ministers administer the provision in relation to the relevant matter` GREATER THAN 1
              THEN JUST `any 1 of the Ministers who administer the provision in relation to the relevant matter`
              ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE IF `how many Ministers administer the provision` EQUALS 1
         THEN JUST `the Minister administering the provision`
         ELSE IF `how many Ministers administer the provision` GREATER THAN 1
              THEN JUST `any 1 of the Ministers who administer the provision`
              ELSE NOTHING

-- src:660 | (3) If a provision of an Act refers to a Minister and specifies the Minister merely by reference to the fact that the Minister administers a specified Act or enactment, subsection (2) applies as if references in paragraphs (a) to (c) to the provision were references to the specified Act or enactment.
@ref s 33(3) (src:660-660)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act refers to a Minister and specifies the Minister merely by reference to the fact that the Minister administers a specified Act or enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (2) applies as if references to the provision were references to the specified Act or enactment (s 33(3))` IS
    IF `a provision of an Act refers to a Minister and specifies the Minister merely by reference to the fact that the Minister administers a specified Act or enactment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:661 | (4) If an Act defines the expression ‘Minister’ or ‘the Minister’ for the purposes of the Act or a provision of the Act in a way that does not specify a particular Minister by title, subsections (2) and (3) apply to the provision despite that definition of the expression.
@ref s 33(4) (src:661-661)
GIVEN `an Act defines the expression Minister or the Minister in a way that does not specify a particular Minister by title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsections (2) and (3) apply to the provision despite the definition (s 33(4))` IS
    IF `an Act defines the expression Minister or the Minister in a way that does not specify a particular Minister by title` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:662 | (5) In an Act, a reference to a specified Minister who no longer exists—
-- src:663 | (a) is a reference to the Minister specified by notification by the Governor in Council; and
@ref s 33(5) (src:662-663)
GIVEN `the specified Minister no longer exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to the specified Minister is a reference to the Minister specified by notification by the Governor in Council (s 33(5)(a))` IS
    IF `the specified Minister no longer exists` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:664 | (b) includes another Minister, or a member of the Executive Council, who is acting for the specified Minister.
@ref s 33(5) (src:664-664)
GIVEN `the specified Minister no longer exists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is another Minister, or a member of the Executive Council, who is acting for the specified Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to the specified Minister includes a reference to the person (s 33(5)(b))` IS
    IF `the specified Minister no longer exists` AND `the person is another Minister, or a member of the Executive Council, who is acting for the specified Minister` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 33AA to 33AC -- departments, chief executives, 2 or more Ministers`

-- src:666 | (1) In an Act, a reference to a department is a reference to an entity that is a department of government under the Public Sector Act 2022.
@ref s 33AA(1) (src:666-666)
GIVEN `the entity is a department of government under the Public Sector Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a department is a reference to the entity (s 33AA(1))` IS
    JUST `the entity is a department of government under the Public Sector Act 2022`

DECLARE `Which department a reference to the department is a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `the department of government that deals with the relevant matter and is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering the provision in relation to the matter`
    `the department of government that deals with the matters to which the provision relates and is administered by the Minister or Ministers for the time being administering the provision`

-- src:667 | (2) In a provision of an Act, a reference to the department without specifying a particular department of government by name is a reference to—
-- src:668 | (a) if, for the time being, different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters—the department of government that—
-- src:669 | (i) deals with the relevant matter; and
-- src:670 | (ii) is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering the provision in relation to the matter; or
-- src:671 | (b) in any other case—the department of government that—
-- src:672 | (i) deals with the matters to which the provision relates; and
-- src:673 | (ii) is administered by the Minister or Ministers for the time being administering the provision.
@ref s 33AA(2) (src:667-673)
GIVEN `the reference specifies a particular department of government by name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which department a reference to the department is a reference to`
DECIDE `which department a reference to the department is a reference to (s 33AA(2))` IS
    IF `the reference specifies a particular department of government by name`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters`
         THEN JUST `the department of government that deals with the relevant matter and is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering the provision in relation to the matter`
         ELSE JUST `the department of government that deals with the matters to which the provision relates and is administered by the Minister or Ministers for the time being administering the provision`

-- src:674 | (3) In an Act, a reference to a specified department of government that no longer exists is a reference to the department specified by notification by the Governor in Council.
@ref s 33AA(3) (src:674-674)
GIVEN `the specified department of government no longer exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to the department is a reference to the department specified by notification by the Governor in Council (s 33AA(3))` IS
    IF `the specified department of government no longer exists` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:675 | (4) If a provision of an Act refers to a department of government and specifies the department by reference to the administration (however described) of a specified Act or enactment, subsection (2) applies as if references in paragraphs (a) and (b) to the provision were references to the specified Act or enactment.
@ref s 33AA(4) (src:675-675)
GIVEN `a provision refers to a department of government and specifies it by reference to the administration (however described) of a specified Act or enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (2) applies as if references to the provision were references to the specified Act or enactment (s 33AA(4))` IS
    IF `a provision refers to a department of government and specifies it by reference to the administration (however described) of a specified Act or enactment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:677 | (1) In an Act, a reference to a chief executive is a reference to a chief executive of a public sector unit.
@ref s 33AB(1) (src:677-677)
GIVEN `the entity is a chief executive of a public sector unit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a chief executive is a reference to the entity (s 33AB(1))` IS
    JUST `the entity is a chief executive of a public sector unit`

DECLARE `Which public sector unit a reference to the chief executive is a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `the public sector unit that deals with the relevant matter and is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering the provision in relation to the matter`
    `the public sector unit that deals with the matters to which the provision relates and is administered by the Minister or Ministers for the time being administering the provision`

-- src:678 | (2) In a provision of an Act, a reference to the chief executive without specifying a particular public sector unit by name is a reference to the chief executive of—
-- src:679 | (a) if, for the time being, different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters—the public sector unit that—
-- src:680 | (i) deals with the relevant matter; and
-- src:681 | (ii) is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering the provision in relation to the matter; or
-- src:682 | (b) in any other case—the public sector unit that—
-- src:683 | (i) deals with the matters to which the provision relates; and
-- src:684 | (ii) is administered by the Minister or Ministers for the time being administering the provision.
@ref s 33AB(2) (src:678-684)
GIVEN `the reference specifies a particular public sector unit by name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Which public sector unit a reference to the chief executive is a reference to`
DECIDE `the chief executive of which public sector unit a reference to the chief executive is a reference to (s 33AB(2))` IS
    IF `the reference specifies a particular public sector unit by name`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `different Ministers administer the provision in relation to different matters`
         THEN JUST `the public sector unit that deals with the relevant matter and is administered by the Minister or Ministers administering the provision in relation to the matter`
         ELSE JUST `the public sector unit that deals with the matters to which the provision relates and is administered by the Minister or Ministers for the time being administering the provision`

-- src:685 | (3) If a provision of an Act refers to a chief executive by reference to the administration (however described) of a specified Act or enactment, subsection (2) applies as if references in paragraph (a) or (b) to the provision were references to the specified Act or enactment.
@ref s 33AB(3) (src:685-685)
GIVEN `a provision refers to a chief executive by reference to the administration (however described) of a specified Act or enactment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (2) applies as if references to the provision were references to the specified Act or enactment (s 33AB(3))` IS
    IF `a provision refers to a chief executive by reference to the administration (however described) of a specified Act or enactment` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:687 | To remove any doubt, it is declared that if—
-- src:688 | (a) a provision of an Act is administered by 2 or more Ministers; and
-- src:689 | (b) under any of sections 33 to 33AB, the provision authorises or requires anything to be done by or in relation to any 1 of the Ministers;
-- src:690 | the provision does not authorise or require it to be done in a particular case by or in relation to more than 1 of the Ministers.
@ref s 33AC (src:687-690)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act is administered by 2 or more Ministers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under any of sections 33 to 33AB, the provision authorises or requires anything to be done by or in relation to any 1 of the Ministers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision authorises or requires it to be done in a particular case by or in relation to more than 1 of the Ministers (s 33AC)` IS
    IF `a provision of an Act is administered by 2 or more Ministers` AND `under any of sections 33 to 33AB, the provision authorises or requires anything to be done by or in relation to any 1 of the Ministers`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 33A -- References to States include Territories`

DECLARE `Territory` IS ONE OF
    `the Australian Capital Territory`
    `the Northern Territory`
    `another Territory`

-- (1): a reference to a State (other than a reference to Queensland or a particular State by name) includes the ACT and the NT.
-- src:692 | (1) In an Act, a reference to a State (other than a reference to Queensland or a particular State by name) includes a reference to the Australian Capital Territory and the Northern Territory.
@ref s 33A(1) (src:692-692)
GIVEN `the reference is a reference to Queensland or to a particular State by name` IS A BOOLEAN
      territory IS A `Territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a State includes a reference to the Territory (s 33A(1))` IS
    IF `the reference is a reference to Queensland or to a particular State by name`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER territory
        WHEN `the Australian Capital Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the Northern Territory` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `another Territory` THEN NOTHING

-- src:696 | (2) Subsection (1) is not displaced merely because there is an express reference to a Territory elsewhere in the Act.
@ref s 33A(2) (src:696-696)
GIVEN `there is an express reference to a Territory elsewhere in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (1) is displaced merely because there is an express reference to a Territory elsewhere in the Act (s 33A(2))` IS
    IF `there is an express reference to a Territory elsewhere in the Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- (3): applies to an Act (other than this Act) enacted before 1 July 1994 only if the Act includes a definition to the effect that a reference to a State includes a reference to a Territory.
-- src:697 | (3) This section applies to an Act (other than this Act) enacted before 1 July 1994 only if the Act includes a definition to the effect that a reference to a State includes a reference to a Territory.
@ref s 33A(3) (src:697-697)
GIVEN `the Act is this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the Act was enacted` IS A DATE
      `the Act includes a definition to the effect that a reference to a State includes a reference to a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33A applies to the Act (s 33A(3))` IS
    IF (NOT `the Act is this Act`) AND `the date the Act was enacted` LESS THAN Date 1 7 1994
    THEN JUST `the Act includes a definition to the effect that a reference to a State includes a reference to a Territory`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 34 to 34B -- officers, chair titles`

-- src:699 | In an Act, a reference to a particular officer, or to the holder of a particular office, includes a reference to the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned.
@ref s 34 (src:699-699)
GIVEN `the reference is to a particular officer, or to the holder of a particular office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference includes a reference to the person for the time being occupying or acting in the office concerned (s 34)` IS
    IF `the reference is to a particular officer, or to the holder of a particular office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:701 | (1) If an Act establishes an office with a chair title (the statutory title), a person holding the office may choose to be referred to by the statutory title or another chair title (the alternative title).
@ref s 34A(1) (src:701-701)
GIVEN `an Act establishes an office with a chair title (the statutory title)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the title chosen is the statutory title or another chair title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person holding the office may choose to be referred to by the title (s 34A(1))` IS
    IF `an Act establishes an office with a chair title (the statutory title)` AND `the title chosen is the statutory title or another chair title` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:702 | (2) For performing functions and exercising powers, it is irrelevant that the person holding the office uses the alternative title.
@ref s 34A(2) (src:702-702)
GIVEN `the person holding the office uses the alternative title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is relevant for performing functions and exercising powers that the person uses the alternative title (s 34A(2))` IS
    IF `the person holding the office uses the alternative title` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

`the titles of chair, chairperson, chairman and chairwoman` MEANS LIST "chair", "chairperson", "chairman", "chairwoman"

-- src:703 | (3) In this section—
-- src:704 | chair title means the title of chair, chairperson, chairman or chairwoman or another similar title.
@ref s 34A(3) (src:703-704)
GIVEN title IS A STRING
      `it is another similar title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the title is a chair title (s 34A(3), definition chair title)` IS
    JUST ((elem title `the titles of chair, chairperson, chairman and chairwoman`) OR `it is another similar title`)

-- src:706 | (1) If an Act establishes an office with a deputy chair title (the statutory title), a person holding the office may choose to be referred to by the statutory title or another deputy chair title (the alternative title).
@ref s 34B(1) (src:706-706)
GIVEN `an Act establishes an office with a deputy chair title (the statutory title)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the title chosen is the statutory title or another deputy chair title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person holding the office may choose to be referred to by the deputy chair title (s 34B(1))` IS
    IF `an Act establishes an office with a deputy chair title (the statutory title)` AND `the title chosen is the statutory title or another deputy chair title` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:707 | (2) For performing functions and exercising powers, it is irrelevant that the person holding the office uses the alternative title.
@ref s 34B(2) (src:707-707)
GIVEN `the person holding the office uses the alternative title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is relevant for performing functions and exercising powers that the person uses the alternative deputy chair title (s 34B(2))` IS
    IF `the person holding the office uses the alternative title` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

`the titles of deputy chair, deputy chairperson, deputy chairman and deputy chairwoman` MEANS LIST "deputy chair", "deputy chairperson", "deputy chairman", "deputy chairwoman"

-- src:708 | (3) In this section—
-- src:709 | deputy chair title means the title of deputy chair, deputy chairperson, deputy chairman or deputy chairwoman or another similar title.
@ref s 34B(3) (src:708-709)
GIVEN title IS A STRING
      `it is another similar title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the title is a deputy chair title (s 34B(3), definition deputy chair title)` IS
    JUST ((elem title `the titles of deputy chair, deputy chairperson, deputy chairman and deputy chairwoman`) OR `it is another similar title`)

§§ `ss 35 and 35A -- Queensland implied, persons with an interest in land`

-- src:711 | (1) In an Act—
-- src:712 | (a) a reference to an officer, office or entity is a reference to such an officer, office or entity in and for Queensland; and
@ref s 35(1) (src:711-712)
GIVEN `the reference is to an officer, office or entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference is a reference to such an officer, office or entity in and for Queensland (s 35(1)(a))` IS
    IF `the reference is to an officer, office or entity` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:713 | (b) a reference to a locality, jurisdiction or other thing is a reference to such a locality, jurisdiction or other thing in and of Queensland.
@ref s 35(1) (src:713-713)
GIVEN `the reference is to a locality, jurisdiction or other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference is a reference to such a locality, jurisdiction or other thing in and of Queensland (s 35(1)(b))` IS
    IF `the reference is to a locality, jurisdiction or other thing` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:714 | (2) In an Act, a reference to an office or entity established by or under an Act need not include the words ‘Queensland’ or ‘of Queensland’ merely because the words form part of its name or title.
@ref s 35(2) (src:714-714)
GIVEN `the office or entity is established by or under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the words Queensland or of Queensland form part of its name or title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference need include the words Queensland or of Queensland (s 35(2))` IS
    IF `the office or entity is established by or under an Act` AND `the words Queensland or of Queensland form part of its name or title` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Capacity in relation to land` IS ONE OF
    proprietor
    transferor
    transferee
    mortgagor
    mortgagee
    lessor
    lessee
    trustee
    `a person having an interest in land`
    `another capacity`

DECLARE `Person who is included` IS ONE OF
    `the person's personal representatives`
    `the person's successors`
    `the person's assigns`
    `anyone else`

-- src:716 | In an Act, a reference to a person as proprietor, transferor, transferee, mortgagor, mortgagee, lessor, lessee, trustee or as having an interest in land includes a reference to the person’s personal representatives, successors and assigns.
@ref s 35A (src:716-716)
GIVEN capacity IS A `Capacity in relation to land`
      included IS A `Person who is included`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a reference to a person in the capacity includes a reference to the person included (s 35A)` IS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN `another capacity` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE CONSIDER included
        WHEN `anyone else` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
